    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The republic was proclaimed on 9 November 1918 during the German Revolution, and its constitution was adopted by a National Assembly that met in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weimar">Weimar</a> in 1919.</li><li>The hyperinflation of 1923 raised the price of a loaf of bread from 3 Reichsmarks in 1922 to 80 billion in November 1923, until the Rentenmark stabilised the currency.</li><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reichstag-fire-decree">Reichstag Fire Decree</a> and the Enabling Act of 23 March 1933 gave Hitler's government power to act outside parliamentary control, which is widely held to mark the end of the republic.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The name &quot;<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weimar-republic">Weimar Republic</a>&quot; was first used by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adolf-hitler">Adolf Hitler</a> in 1929; officially the state kept the name German Reich, and the term only became mainstream in the 1950s.</p></aside>
    </section>

